{"type":"assistant","uuid":"601c7a48-543c-42d4-8e4a-2e051c5e9ce3","session_id":"63d4a3ec-8183-43b0-af23-73fa635d8185","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"601c7a48-543c-42d4-8e4a-2e051c5e9ce3","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The fix is in place and correct. Let me summarize what was done.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"61c12336-7613-4b72-878c-516665936409","session_id":"63d4a3ec-8183-43b0-af23-73fa635d8185","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"61c12336-7613-4b72-878c-516665936409","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The bug is fixed. Here's a summary:\n\n## Diagnosis\n\n**Root cause:** The `ParticipantTabActivity` is a `ListFragment` that stores a selected participant in a long-press `ActionMode`. When the user swipes to a different tab **while the ActionMode is still active**, the fragment is destroyed/detached, making `getActivity()` return `null`. Subsequently, clicking a menu item (e.g., \"create payment\") triggers `onActionItemClicked` → `getApp()` → `getActivity().getApplication()`, causing the `NullPointerException`.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdded a null check at the top of `MyActionModeCallback.onActionItemClicked()`. If `getActivity()` returns `null` (fragment detached), the ActionMode is gracefully finished and the action is not handled:\n\n```java\nif (getActivity() == null) {\n    mode.finish();\n    return false;\n}\n```\n\nThis prevents the NPE and correctly dismisses the stale action mode when the user navigates away from the fragment."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":30201,"output_tokens":238,"cache_read_input_tokens":23232,"total_tokens":30439}}}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"0b94a450-bf91-4642-a15b-b63fd17361e7","session_id":"63d4a3ec-8183-43b0-af23-73fa635d8185","is_error":false,"duration_ms":42418,"duration_api_ms":31684,"num_turns":6,"result":"The bug is fixed. Here's a summary:\n\n## Diagnosis\n\n**Root cause:** The `ParticipantTabActivity` is a `ListFragment` that stores a selected participant in a long-press `ActionMode`. When the user swipes to a different tab **while the ActionMode is still active**, the fragment is destroyed/detached, making `getActivity()` return `null`. Subsequently, clicking a menu item (e.g., \"create payment\") triggers `onActionItemClicked` → `getApp()` → `getActivity().getApplication()`, causing the `NullPointerException`.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdded a null check at the top of `MyActionModeCallback.onActionItemClicked()`. If `getActivity()` returns `null` (fragment detached), the ActionMode is gracefully finished and the action is not handled:\n\n```java\nif (getActivity() == null) {\n    mode.finish();\n    return false;\n}\n```\n\nThis prevents the NPE and correctly dismisses the stale action mode when the user navigates away from the fragment.","usage":{"input_tokens":157227,"output_tokens":2455,"cache_read_input_tokens":110880,"total_tokens":159682},"permission_denials":[]}
